    "b-10-operator-runbook-the-left-rail-is-five-nu-7": {
      "id": "b-10-operator-runbook-the-left-rail-is-five-nu-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The left rail is five numbered lifecycle stage cards (the pipeline rail).\nEach card is a vertical slice: a header with the stage's one-line verdict,\nits detail rows, its own buttons, and its disclosures. The current stage has\nthe filled number chip and bright border; disabled buttons carry the\nblocking reason in their tooltip and the one recommended next action is\nhighlighted."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-operator-runbook-stage-detail-rows-8": {
      "id": "b-10-operator-runbook-stage-detail-rows-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| Stage | Detail rows | Healthy verdict | Owns |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 Sync | Branch (dirty marker), Baseline freshness | "
        },
        {
          "insert": "up to date with origin/master",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | Sync Merged PRs (locked while a run is active) |\n| 2 Run | Workers, claims/checkpoints, last Save point | "
        },
        {
          "insert": "active · N active claims",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " while working, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "paused · 0 active claims",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " before handoff | Start Working, Pause Intake, Resume, Stop, Force Stop; Setup + Process disclosures |\n| 3 Ship | Checkpoint lanes, Branch QA (informational; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "blocked",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " = rework readmitted at repair priority, never a PR gate), Ship set (THE PR gate), Plan | "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr_ready — N confirmed match(es)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | Prepare Handoff (the whole pipeline incl. auto-reconcile, PR board seed, and the hard "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ship",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " save point — it ends the session); Manual steps (Run QA, Resolve QA Repair, Reconcile, Plan PRs — debug escape hatches; checkpointing is automatic) + Artifacts disclosure |\n| 4 PRs | One row per tracked slice PR (status, #, comments, CI), upstream open count | "
        },
        {
          "insert": "N open · M to open · K merged",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Draft PR Board",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — a six-column kanban (Planned → Preparing → Prepared → Draft → In Review → Done) reflecting derived per-slice state; in-flight prep and QA-repair-pending slices show in Preparing, review substate (awaiting/new comments/changes requested/fixing) drives the In Review chip + Ack/Fixing controls. Sync PR Status (gh-backed; records persist in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr_handoff/pr_records.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "); "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/api/prs/review-state",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for manual review flags |\n| 5 New Session | — | "
        },
        {
          "insert": "restart baseline · keep local work",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | New Session (checkpoints first; unshipped improvements stay local) |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
